# Test: a BGP peer whose authenticated BFD profile would join an unauthenticated session is refused
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 5882 Section 10.2 -- "BFD authentication SHOULD be used and
#            is strongly encouraged." One session carries one authentication
#            configuration. A pinned single-hop session to 127.0.0.254 runs
#            under the profile open (no auth block); a strict BGP peer to the
#            same neighbor from the same local address names the profile
#            secure (Keyed SHA1). The peer's EnsureSession is refused with an
#            error that says the authentication differs, why (every client of
#            one remote system shares one BFD session, RFC 5882 Section 4.4),
#            and a fix that works even when OSPF, whose bfd block carries no
#            authentication, shares the session (drop this client's auth block,
#            or give every other client the same one and disable bfd on any
#            OSPF interface to the neighbor), and the session is not shared.
# PREVENTS:  a client that asked for BFD authentication running on a session
#            that has none, with no word to the operator.
#
# Method: a native Go fixture boots ze with the config, waits for the pinned
# session, the strict peer held down by the refusal and the mismatch text, with
# its reason and fix, on stderr, and rejects any line saying the session was shared or opened for the
# peer.

option=env:var=ze.bfd.test-parallel:value=true
# BFD binds the RFC 5881 fixed ports; see test/plugin/bgp-bfd-opt-in.ci.
option=exclusive:group=bfd-ports

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/bgp-bfd-auth-join-refused:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=bfd strict-mode EnsureSession failed; peer is held down
expect=stderr:contains=BFD authentication differs from that of the live session to the same neighbor: the live session runs no authentication but this client's bfd profile
expect=stderr:contains=every client of one remote system shares one BFD session (RFC 5882 Section 4.4)
expect=stderr:contains=to fix it, remove the auth block from this client's bfd profile
expect=stderr:contains=or give every other client of this neighbor a bfd profile with the same auth { type; key-id; secret; } block and, on every OSPF interface to this neighbor, set bfd { enabled false; } or delete its bfd block, because an OSPF interface's bfd block carries no authentication
expect=stderr:contains=a live session keeps the authentication it was built with until every client has released it
expect=stderr:contains=a refused client asks again when it next starts BFD
reject=stderr:contains=bfd session shared
